        "text_MkLUJr": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h5>The Cut and Shape of a diamond are distinct yet interrelated. When using the term Shape, we are essentially referencing the silhouette, or outline, as seen from the top of the diamond. While Cut refers to the overall arrangement of the stone's facets and the way light is reflected through them. Put simply, Shape is an aesthetic choice, and Cut contributes most to how beautifully a gemstone sparkles.</h5>",
